      "cooked": "<p>So, in my game today playing Akash'Bhuta in the Pike Industrial Complex, Disrupt the field was drawn from the Villain deck.</p><blockquote><p>Disrupt the field</p><p>Destroy All Environment cards.</p><p>Play the top card of the Villain deck.</p><p>Play the top card of the Environment deck.</p></blockquote><p>Chemical Explosion was the Environment card that was drawn.</p><blockquote><p>Chemical Explosion</p><p>Destroy All Vat Cards</p><p>Deal each target X toxic damage . . .&nbsp;</p><p>At the End of the Environment turn, destroy this card.</p></blockquote><p>So, it did it's thing but hung around because it wasn't the End of the Environment turn. &nbsp;When it came around to the Environment turn, a Vat card was drawn. &nbsp;Does this Vat card being drawn activate Chemical Explosion again? &nbsp;Is the Vat card destroyed? &nbsp;Does everyone take damage again?</p>",
